#21600
Credits Room~
    The Garden of Xinge was written by Robert Hayden <hayden@pobox.com>
for Ravenmud.  It is the first part of the overall City of Xinge area,
which is actually several zones.  The garden and its tower is outside, and
the city is beyond the garden's gates.  
    The Garden's purpose is two-fold.  First it islargely a basic,
medium-risk xp area.  11 different plant varieties are offered.  Second,
in the center of the garden is a large magic tower, with 12 very
heavy-duty mobs in it, and appropriate eq, guarded by a 4-headed Dragon
named Cabal.
    None of the plants wander, and only a couple are aggro.  The Yellow
Musk Zombies, made by the creepers, do wander around the zone.
    As it is, I made sure every one of the 69 rooms outside of the central
tower have plants in them, all varieties in seemingly random locations.
    One of the intersting plants is the Bloodvine.  The heart is towards
the middle of the garden.  However, in each room is a "runner", showing
the plant spreading out all over the garden.
    I liked making this zone; I think it's better than my ant colony
(although the room descriptions were purposly left pretty generic, in
this type of zone, nobody reads them anyways.)  I like it for the huge
variety of mobs here, including one that covers the entire zone :-)  For
that plant, I had each "runner" load, if-flagged to the main "heart" of
the plant. Thus, to get each runner to repop, you would have to kill the
heart of the plant (the heart is limited to one incarnation).  Thought it
was an interesting approach. Hope it works ;-)
    The Tower of Xinge is in the center of the garen. The goal of this
tower was for good run, with tough mobs, and good EQ for everyone (much
like the Abyss).  What I've got is 12 mobs of heavy strength (45th
level), with the last bastard being an ugly wizard (50th level).  1 of
each class is present in each of the 10 wings of the tower, with the key
from one room leading to the next (hence, you have 10 rooms to go through
to get to the end).  Originally written as a seperate zone (The Tower of
Dread), but it has been modified and patched into the Garden of Xinge.
    On the north side of the garden is a gate which will eventually lead
to the next zone (the city itself).  The key to the gate can be either
purchased from the gatekeeper, or the gatekeeper can be killed for the key
Currently, the gate described as an "E", but doesn't go anywhere.  A sign
on the gate explains.
~
